<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSE SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP CLOSE SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the second</p>
<p>day of four-day English county championship matches on Friday:</p>
<p>Leeds (Headingley): Yorkshire 166 (J.Taylor 6-45) and 74-0.</p>
<p>Northamptonshire 286 (K.Curran 63, R.Bailey 61; C.Silverwood</p>
<p>4-62).</p>
<p>Colwyn Bay: Nottinghamshire 165-9 (M.Dowman 62) v Glamorgan.</p>
<p>Colchester: Essex 533-8 declared (S.Law 175, N.Hussein 128,</p>
<p>A.Grayson 81, R.Irani 76). Leicestershire 18-2.</p>
<p>Chester-le-Street: Derbyshire 254 and 176 (M.May 64; S.Brown</p>
<p>5-58). Durham 174 (P.DeFreitas 5-37) and 48-3.</p>
<p>Worcester: Worcestershire 409-7 (D.Leatherdale 120 not out,</p>
<p>V.Solanki 61, T.Moody 60) v Kent.</p>
<p>Birmingham (Edgbaston): Warwickshire 227 (M.Wagh 57;</p>
<p>M.Robinson 4-53, V.Drakes 4-84). Sussex 63 (A.Donald 4-11) and</p>
<p>7-2.</p>
